From 658e9ff3171d00ca4b37e341d4b7403a6cb0c0e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aeon <171243930+aeon1911@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 18:09:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/64] Switch: steadier frame rate in scenes with lots of
 fire, torches and effects.

- Frame rate stabilizer (nx_stabilizer = target FPS): while frames miss the
  target it trims only visual load step by step (fewer dynamic lights,
  distant effects/particles, near-invisible effects, sprite shadow range,
  dynamic light on sprites) and brings detail back slowly afterwards.
- Dynamic light budget (nx_dynlight_max/nx_dynlight_dist): only the lights
  nearest to the camera are used; the others fade out instead of popping.
- Identical light data is not re-uploaded for every wall/flat (the driver
  re-sends the whole constant buffer on each upload).
- Mipmaps are built on the CPU: glGenerateMipmap goes through Mesa's blitter
  with a full state save/restore per level, which made every new texture
  cost milliseconds. Prefetched sprites now get their mipmaps at upload time
  instead of from glGenerateMipmap in the middle of drawing.
- SDL's threads (audio mixing for OpenAL) run on core 2 instead of competing
  with the game thread on core 0 (from nx3.8).
- perf.log: GL draw calls, dynamic lights used/total, light uploads skipped,
  stabilizer level; FPS limiter sleep counts as waiting.
- Version uz5.0.3-nx4.1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
